= Public-key cryptography — Technical =

An asymmetric scheme generates a key pair (pk,sk) such that specified operations using pk and sk are complementary while recovering sk from pk is computationally infeasible under the scheme's security assumptions. Security must be stated against a formal adversary model; possession of pk alone does not identify its controller.

== Modeling / security cautions ==
* public-key cryptography ≠ encryption only
* public key ≠ identity proof by itself
* public-key cryptography ≠ blockchain

